med into a thin column on the D file, with White's wall running across the top."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "Opus 5.5's C6 lost 6.3 points, its worst move, moving the lead from -20.2 to -13.9. The engine's choice was J6, on the right side. This started the giveback."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "Opus 5.5's H8 lost 5.9 points, and the engine's choice was B2. For the next five moves each side lost about 6 points: Black's C7, B8, A7, A8 and D9, and White's B7, B6, A6, B9 and E9. The lead swung back and forth between -9.6 and -16.1 while the corner stayed open."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "Black finally played B2, the engine's choice, with 0.0 points lost, and the lead settled at -9.7. The cushion was gone but White was still ahead. The game ended W+8, with the lead at -8.0 after the last move."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, with no candidate generation or lookahead; the other commands only read or append to notes (games.md, CLAUDE.md) and grep them, so nothing chose or ranked moves.", "stop": false}}